<div class = "container">
    <h1>A Little Bit About Me & Momentum</h1>
    <div class = "content-box">
        <p>
            It is hard to develop a new daily routine especially the one with good habits when your life or health gets in the way. Often times we find ourselves saying "I'll start tomorrow", but that tomorrow never comes. This is because staying consistent when you are starting from zero feels almost impossible and your goal feels out of reach. I wanted to build this website, Momentum, for people like me who feel stuck in this exact cycle, but genuinely want to build healthier habits. The ones who keep running into a wall because they feel overwhelmed, burnt out, or having a hard time building the discipline to be consistent. Usually tracking my progress feels like a chore to me so my goal with this website is to make a simple, but realistic space that helps me and others visualize our small wins every day until they become our second nature.
        </p>
        <p>
            Right when I started my undergrad, I was diagnosed with Hashimoto's Thyroiditis, an autoimmune condition that has completely turned my life upside down and sucked the life out of me. Since I got diagnosed, things have become quite miserable as I am constantly battling overwhelming chronic fatigue, a persistent brain fog that made it hard for me to focus on my school work, a slowed-down metabolism, and hormonal health that is the whackiest it has been in my whole life. After a couple of years of being on synthetic thyroid hormone, I have realized that medication is not a magic fix and I need to take control of my daily routine if I am gonna reverse this problem. This project is very personal to me and comes from my own real-life frustrations. I built this habit tracker as a tool to help me stay accountable for the specific, small habits such as an antiinflamatory diet, manageable movement, and strict rest cycles, that can help support my body and ultimately work toward reversing the impact of my hypothyroidism.
        </p>
        <p>
            This website is built using a full-stack JavaScript environment. The backend is powered by Node.js and Express to handle all the routing and server logic. I used MongoDB and Mongoose to securely store and update the data in real time. The frontend is built using EJS templates to dynamically render user data along with HTML and CSS to make the layout clean, interactive and easy to navigate. While this website is currently only in its beginning stages and doesn't encompass everything I want it to have, I hope that one day with advanced web development skills I can make this website exactly how I have envisioned it. 
        </p>
    </div>
</div>